Z||000000||Gonzo_442||11-16-2000||12:30 AM||||greetings folks,<P>my set of wheels recently decided it didn't like the belt, and well, long story short, i was sitting on the road, no water pump, no alternator, etc.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>its a v6, 87GT auto. my question is, it limped home (about 30 or so city blocks) 4-5 blocks at a time (when temp hit redzone, i shut it off until it cooled off). the temp light came on only two or three times after the initial blow.<P>first, could there be any damage done to the engine, it had been running for a while before the belt went (half hour, open road), and when it did, it redzoned immediately. it also did a lot of screeching right before it snapped. or is there something that could have caused this?<P>second, it is going in the shop for a belt replacement and general tuneup/overhaul. should i have my mech look at anything else?<BR>tuneup/overhaul encompases: new plugs, new wires, new oil/filter, new tranny fluid/filter, brake check (possible pads, etc.), coolant flush and fill, new rad hoses, new battery and cables.<P>as a side note, i fished out the belt, it looks like it's been chewed on by a rather large dog. i've seen worn belts, but this is the first one i've ever had that went. usually i get to them first :/<BR>is it normal for it to look like this?<P>------------------<BR>--<BR>Gonzo_442<BR>1987 GT, soon to be archie'd||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||11-16-2000||09:16 AM||||Well, 'fit were me, I'd reach down and see if the water pump and alternator pulleys turn freely.  One of them might have seized, causing the belt failure.<P>Fortunately, the OE V6 is all iron (block and heads), so it would tend to be relatively heat tolerant.  A pressure test of the cooling system, and a compression check or blowdown test probably wouldn't be a bad idea at this point.   <P>Belts are definitely not supposed to look chewed up.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ralfy9862||11-16-2000||09:21 AM||||same happend to mine last week i changed the water pump and belt and i was fine my belt also looked chewed up and the water pump was the reason why it happened||||reg||13
Z||000003||fiero56||11-16-2000||10:04 AM||||My SE liked to chew up belts. Turns out the water pump pulley was slightly bent. Since I had a spare pulley, I just replaced the pulley. No problems so far. The belts were really chewed up from that bent pulley.||||reg||1
